Why this file exists, and how to read its result.

The first component campaign returned:

    UNSCORED  proxy join dropped   -- "FAIL: no tests matched 'FlowViz'"
    killed    payload writer dropped
    SURVIVED  IDENTITY CONTROL     (correct)

An UNSCORED re-run ALONE proves nothing -- repo memory
rerun-unknowns-with-controls. If arm 1 is re-run by itself and scores, there is
no way to tell whether the mutant is genuinely killed or whether the
environment merely cooperated this time. So both already-scored siblings ride
along with KNOWN expected verdicts. Three outcomes, three conclusions:

  siblings reproduce (killed / SURVIVED) AND arm 1 scores
      -> the environment is sound and arm 1's new verdict is the real one.
         The first "no tests matched" was a transient.

  siblings reproduce AND arm 1 is UNSCORED again
      -> the fault is specific to THIS mutant, not the environment. Most
         likely the mutant makes the module fail to load, so the filter
         matches nothing -- an INVALID-shaped result wearing UNSCORED's
         clothes, and it needs reading as such, not as a survivor.

  siblings do NOT reproduce
      -> the whole run is untrustworthy and NOTHING in it is a verdict,
         including arm 1. Fix the environment before drawing any conclusion.

The identity control is last, as always: if it does not SURVIVE, the harness is
scoring noise and every other line is void.

The rationale lives here rather than at the top of the .txt because
parse_mutants.py splits on `%%` and raises ValueError on any record that is not
exactly three `--`-separated fields. A prose header would abort the campaign.
